1
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,657
YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:28,537
YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:29,520
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,500
You're on the move!

5
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,320
It's time to duel!

6
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:03,770
Mr.

7
00:01:03,853 --> 00:01:06,400
Kaiba, uh, welcome back, sir.

8
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:08,500
What an unexpected surprise.

9
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:11,528
Yes, I'm sure it is,
you treacherous snakes.

10
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:12,970
You see,

11
00:01:13,053 --> 00:01:15,257
I know all about your
partnership with Pegasus

12
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:18,340
and the scheme you had to
take over my corporation.

13
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:19,630
That's right!

14
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:22,160
What you guys did was really messed up!

15
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:24,410
Mukuba...

16
00:01:24,493 --> 00:01:27,865
Working with that creep to try
and get rid of my brother and me?

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,440
You guys are sick!

18
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:32,080
You're all fired,

19
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:34,817
and I suggest you leave
now before I really

20
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:37,920
lose my temper and take
more than just your jobs.

21
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:39,600
But let us explain.

22
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,760
Don't test me, you slime.

23
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:47,132
Seto, if you simply let us speak, you'll
understand why we did what we did.

24
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:48,130
That I doubt.

25
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:52,117
The sole reason we formed this
so-called partnership with Master...

26
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,200
Pardon, Mr.

27
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:54,697
Pegasus, was to rescue you.

28
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:57,077
Yes, Johnson here is absolutely right.

29
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,677
Pegasus was the one who
wanted your company,

30
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:03,077
and we thought that perhaps if we had
some sort of phony alliance with him,

31
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,457
it would lead us to you.

32
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:06,640
You expect us to believe that?

33
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:10,337
Seto, we had no intention
of taking over Kyber Corp.

34
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:11,250
In fact,

35
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:15,137
we've been waiting for your stamp of approval
before we sent out our latest product.

36
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,540
It's your VirtuaPod.

37
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,132
We've readied it for market distribution.

38
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:20,930
You have?

39
00:02:21,013 --> 00:02:21,843
Impressive.

40
00:02:21,926 --> 00:02:24,157
But don't think that that
means you're off the hook.

41
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,070
Any of you.

42
00:02:25,153 --> 00:02:26,600
Yeah, you tell him.

43
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:30,720
At last, Mokuba, my virtual
adventure game is ready to be tested.

44
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:34,520
Wait, Seto!

45
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:42,040
You just got back.

46
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,477
Why do you have to try it out right now?

47
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,577
You don't need to worry about it, Mokuba.

48
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:48,013
But it could be a trap!

49
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,717
You're forgetting, little brother.

50
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:52,976
I designed each and every
program in this game myself.

51
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:59,739
You know how long I've been
waiting for this moment.

52
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:02,220
And now it's finally here.

53
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,080
Isn't it beautiful?

54
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,360
And it's finished at last.

55
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:23,640
Insert dueling deck into
the drive recognizer.

56
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,217
All systems go.

57
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:31,594
Virtua screen closing.

58
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,660
Get ready, Mokuba.

59
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:38,697
Virtua screen locked.

60
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,300
Reality uplink loading.

61
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:44,100
Big Brother, are you positive
about this? Absolutely.

62
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:45,560
Now start it up.

63
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,300
Okay then.

64
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:49,320
I won't be long, Mokuba.

65
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,900
Oh, I hope he knows what he's doing.

66
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,320
Be careful

67
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:03,957
This mine transport portal
has certainly been smoothed

68
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:08,840
out I can hardly even feel the
separation from my body Now,

69
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,820
let's see how the virtual world itself is

70
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:28,137
Visuals, check.

71
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:29,080
Sounds, check.

72
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:30,657
Life points, check.

73
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:31,760
So far, so good.

74
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:34,660
Maybe I was wrong.

75
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:35,877
He's okay.

76
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,060
So far.

77
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:44,490
Excellent.

78
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:46,033
Just like I programmed.

79
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:51,200
I summon the Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

80
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,840
White lightning attack!

81
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:01,750
Huh?

82
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,920
The armed ninja?

83
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,620
I didn't design this. Attack!

84
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:11,850
What?

85
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:14,480
A dragon capture jar?

86
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:16,890
No!

87
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:20,631
Someone must have reprogrammed
the game's combat protocols!

88
00:05:22,020 --> 00:05:24,760
My blue eyes! No! Huh?

89
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:31,940
Something's wrong! Settle!

90
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,780
Big Brother!

91
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,640
Are you okay?

92
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:51,880
Say something!

93
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:59,977
Your brother's obsession with technology
has always been his greatest weakness.

94
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:00,997
What did you do?

95
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:03,577
Seto should have heeded
your warning, little Mokuma.

96
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:07,397
But now it's too late and his mind
is imprisoned in his own game.

97
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:11,020
Yes, thanks to a few technical
modifications we've made.

98
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,620
And with you our prisoner once again,

99
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:17,174
there'll be no one to stop
us from taking over Kaibokor.

100
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:18,540
Little brother.

101
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,400
Enter the access code.

102
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:36,420
Where'd that brat go?

103
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:39,816
He went through the ventilator shaft.

104
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,220
Kid thinks fast.

105
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:44,600
Mokuba's escaped.

106
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,280
What escaped?

107
00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:49,160
Well, find him, you idiot. Relax.

108
00:06:49,940 --> 00:06:52,260
We don't have to find little Mokuba.

109
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,277
He'll come back to us soon enough.

110
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,420
Why is that?

111
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:57,347
Because we have his brother,

112
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,257
and if Mokuba wants to save him,

113
00:06:59,340 --> 00:07:02,837
the only way is to use the Virtuopod
and beat the game he's trapped in.

114
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:06,680
A scenario that I assure
you is quite unlikely.

115
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:09,960
I'll take it.

116
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,651
Put it on my tab, Gramps.

117
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:13,580
Your tab's past due, Joey.

118
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:15,017
Then put it on Tristan's.

119
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:15,930
Hey.

120
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,030
Huh?

121
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:22,200
Please, please help me. Mokuba!

122
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:28,897
So you're saying the only way Kaiba
can escape is by winning the game?

123
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:33,117
But if those creeps reprogram the entire
adventure just to keep Kaiba trapped there,

124
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:34,435
how is that possible?

125
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:36,297
I don't know, but I thought...

126
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:37,960
I thought you could help.

127
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:39,960
Calm down, Mokuba.

128
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,200
We will, we will.

129
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:45,538
Now tell us some more about this
Virtuopod your brother was designing.

130
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:47,080
I don't know much.

131
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,237
I was pretty young when he started it.

132
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:52,597
I remember him spending endless
hours working on the prototypes,

133
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,209
trying to make it perfect.

134
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:55,710
Prototypes?

135
00:07:55,793 --> 00:07:57,092
So there are other ones?

136
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,880
Mm-hmm. In his lab.

137
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:03,717
It was my brother's dream to create the
world's ultimate virtual adventure land.

138
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:06,918
But those corporate jerks
turned it into a nightmare.

139
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:08,280
Eh, eh.

140
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:09,680
Lousy suits.

141
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:12,740
We'll show them like we did Pegasus. Huh?

142
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:14,330
That's right.

143
00:08:14,413 --> 00:08:18,397
We'll use those Pog prototypes, go to
that virtual world and rescue Kaiba.

144
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,420
Thanks, guys.

145
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:22,407
We'll be back soon, Grandpa.

146
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:24,900
You be careful. We will.

147
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:26,470
Wait up.

148
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:28,501
You guys don't even know the way.

149
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:32,740
Just when I think I can't be
any prouder of those four kids.

150
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,220
This is it.

151
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:36,301
My brother's personal laboratory.

152
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:41,482
He doesn't like anyone messing around in
here, but I used to sneak in all the time.

153
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:49,010
This way.

154
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:55,065
This is where Seto keeps
his most secret stuff.

155
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:01,700
There they are.

156
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:05,080
Those are the prototypes? Wow.

157
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,380
Now let's see here.

158
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:11,120
Yep, just like the model my brother's in.

159
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,500
Only three pods.

160
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:14,477
I guess someone's staying here.

161
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:15,560
I say Tristan.

162
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,200
And I say you.

163
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,820
I know I'm going.

164
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,230
Oh, Koopa.

165
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:22,817
You're the one who knows
how to work these things.

166
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:23,957
You should stay here.

167
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:24,870
Yeah,

168
00:09:24,953 --> 00:09:28,517
but I also know the most about the virtual
adventure land that we're going into.

169
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,360
Good point. So then get in.

170
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:32,860
Take care of my gorgeous bod, pal.

171
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,384
You guys had better be careful.

172
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,020
We'll be fine, Paya.

173
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,997
Yeah, don't you worry about a thing.

174
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,137
We'll have Kaiba rescued in no time.

175
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:43,480
Tristan, let her rip.

176
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:45,440
Right, here we go.

177
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:52,640
Virtual upload now!

178
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,620
Looks like it worked.

179
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:03,780
Ah, the Kaiba Labs building.

180
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:07,840
You see, Mokuba came back
just like I said he would.

181
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:11,077
Yes, but he brought Yukimoto
and those others with him.

182
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:11,990
Don't worry.

183
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:16,697
Once Kimo goes down there and unplugs those
pods, they'll have no way of returning.

184
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:17,721
Not with anyone.

185
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:22,897
I'm glad I've got my dueling deck with me,

186
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:25,637
but this life point count
makes me a bit nervous.

187
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:28,477
I mean, I know what happens in a
video game when you lose a life,

188
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:30,357
but I wonder what happens here.

189
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:31,852
Kind of a scary thought.

190
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:32,900
No joke, Uke.

191
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:37,580
Oh, speaking of scary.

192
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:42,220
It's hard to believe all of
this is virtual and not real.

193
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:45,566
Yeah, well, it looks
plenty real enough to me.

194
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,160
Yeah, zombie alert!

195
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:08,020
Wait a sec.

196
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:10,837
These zombies are nothing
but dual monsters.

197
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,120
So if I just draw a card, then...

198
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:16,660
Then I really don't know what.

199
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,725
Let me show you how it's done.

200
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,720
I summon the Rude Kaiser!

201
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:27,480
And I summon the Dark Magician!

202
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:34,130
Attack!

203
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:46,532
So that's how you do it in Virtual World.

204
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:47,770
They're back!

205
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:49,480
I got them.

206
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:54,720
I summon the Flame Swordsman!

207
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:57,220
Go, Flaming Sword of Battle!

208
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,110
Joey!

209
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,557
Cancel your Flame Swordsman's attack!

210
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:05,470
Hurry!

211
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:10,980
Got dragons reforming again!

212
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,220
What is going on here?

213
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:23,748
Every time we slay one of these zombie
monsters, they come back even stronger.

214
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:24,970
That's true.

215
00:12:25,053 --> 00:12:29,527
But no matter how strong their attacks
get, they still have one major weakness.

216
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:31,169
Just think about it, Joey.

217
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:33,515
Remember, you've defeated them before.

218
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,860
Oh, yeah.

219
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:39,560
Zombies have zero defense power.

220
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,918
So by activating shield and sword...

221
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:49,252
I can reverse their attack and defense
points so their attack becomes zero.

222
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:52,420
Okay, they're all yours, Yugi.

223
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:55,060
Go, Dark Magic Attack!

224
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:01,500
All right!

225
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:05,240
Yugi, check this out.

226
00:13:06,680 --> 00:13:08,560
Hey, what do you think it is?

227
00:13:08,780 --> 00:13:10,897
It must be part of some
kind of scoring system.

228
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:13,920
Hey, my life points aren't going back up.

229
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:16,100
That sure can't be good, can it?

230
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:19,926
Man, I guess these virtual monsters
are playing for keeps, huh?

231
00:13:24,460 --> 00:13:25,700
What is that thing?

232
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:27,630
Hey,

233
00:13:27,713 --> 00:13:32,321
I bet it's one of them fairies that they
put in these games to help the players out.

234
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:34,200
Quick, let's follow it!

235
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:37,900
I can't keep up!

236
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:43,340
That slippery little Sprite.

237
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:44,900
Ah, look!

238
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:46,938
What is it, Mokuba?

239
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,030
Did you find them?

240
00:13:48,113 --> 00:13:51,177
No, but I think I found what
it was trying to show us.

241
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:53,720
Whoa, it's an entire virtual town.

242
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:54,996
Let's go explore it.

243
00:13:57,880 --> 00:14:00,700
Ah, I'm glad we all
ate before we got here.

244
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:02,175
Check this out, Joey.

245
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:03,090
Huh?

246
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:05,450
Cool.

247
00:14:05,533 --> 00:14:07,160
Hey, this might come in handy here.

248
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:08,130
We'll take it.

249
00:14:08,213 --> 00:14:10,356
I don't think that it works that way.

250
00:14:10,540 --> 00:14:11,370
Huh?

251
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:14,980
2,000 points?

252
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:19,680
Ah, well, we must have scored at
least that many from those zombies.

253
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:21,710
Five?

254
00:14:21,793 --> 00:14:22,680
Not even close!

255
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,817
Come on, guys, let's concentrate
on finding my brother first.

256
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:26,730
Hmm.

257
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,277
Okay, you're right.

258
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,797
Let's split up and comb
this town for clues.

259
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:32,280
Search every street.

260
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,600
Question every virtual person you see.

261
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:40,337
Somebody must have spotted him or know
something about what happened to him.

262
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:42,320
Someone, somewhere, can help us.

263
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:44,522
That's the way these games work.

264
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:48,055
When we're done, let's meet
back at the water fountain.

265
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,380
So, Joey, did you find out anything?

266
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:53,060
Yeah, I found out I hate virtual dogs.

267
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:55,420
You guys, I got a great lead.

268
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:57,437
See that mountain? Well,

269
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:59,977
an old woman I was talking
to said that she saw

270
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:02,797
a man with a prisoner
headed there this morning.

271
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:05,617
Supposedly, there's some kind
of ancient temple at the top.

272
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:08,717
And the only way to get there
is by crossing this desert.

273
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:09,630
Great.

274
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,132
So where's our ride out?

275
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,300
Wait for us!

276
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:16,400
Hey, us includes me.

277
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:20,760
I gotta hand it to your brother.

278
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,697
This virtual sand, it
tastes just like real sand.

279
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:24,839
We should go back.

280
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:25,822
It's too rough.

281
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:27,220
No, we can't.

282
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:28,634
We have to keep going.

283
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,560
It's a sand twister.

284
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:33,720
Brace yourselves.

285
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:35,840
It's coming right towards us.

286
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:49,380
Yugi, you, wake up, pal. We're alive.

287
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:52,100
What happened?

288
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:54,772
That sand twister blew us back into town.

289
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:57,666
I think it shook the
little guy up a bit, too.

290
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,220
He'll be okay.

291
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:06,689
That ain't no way to
be crossing no desert.

292
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:10,017
Wait, are you saying you
know how to cross it, then?

293
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:11,537
No, it's not me who knows.

294
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:14,149
It's them desert-crossing
nuatory chickens.

295
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,150
Them what?

296
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:19,300
Oh, you mean the nuatory
card. Thanks, mister.

297
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:21,857
Could you please tell us where
we could go to get a card?

298
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:24,660
I wish I could, but they can't be gotten.

299
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:26,055
They can only be won.

300
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:28,320
Hmm, man, this guy's an odd bird.

301
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:29,780
You say prized bird?

302
00:16:30,020 --> 00:16:32,140
It sure is, especially around here.

303
00:16:33,060 --> 00:16:35,537
I can't figure out what
he's trying to tell us.

304
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:39,032
Maybe one of the card stands
we saw on the way in has one.

305
00:16:39,180 --> 00:16:40,060
Yeah, maybe.

306
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:42,320
It's worth a try.

307
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:44,997
There certainly are plenty
of card stands in this town.

308
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:47,080
Surely one of them has to have it.

309
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:49,260
This is it, men.

310
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,380
Kaiba's private lab.

311
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:55,172
Now it's just a matter of
pulling the plug on those brats.

312
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:57,157
They've been gone a long time.

313
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:58,337
I hope they're okay.

314
00:16:58,420 --> 00:16:59,361
Don't you worry.

315
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,077
I once saw Joy play a video game for three

316
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:04,631
days straight without blinking or nothing.

317
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,710
Really?

318
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:06,710
Figures.

319
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:10,917
Taya, I know what'll make all
this waiting around go by faster.

320
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:11,920
A game.

321
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:14,276
And it's called Guess My Facial Hair.

322
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:15,290
Go right ahead.

323
00:17:15,373 --> 00:17:16,203
Ew.

324
00:17:16,286 --> 00:17:17,200
Uh, I think I'll pass.

325
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,760
Aw, come on.

326
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,037
Don't tell me you haven't
noticed my fine beard growing in.

327
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:23,826
I've got like eight whiskers.

328
00:17:23,940 --> 00:17:24,999
Here, take a feel.

329
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:26,160
Tristan, please.

330
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:30,180
Why don't you just go and
take a nap in the corner? Huh?

331
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:33,877
Yeah, we'll get a bonus for this.

332
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:37,195
Looks to me like we've got
some company headed our way.

333
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:41,037
Quick, let's lock the door and set up
some kind of barricade to hold them off.

334
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,220
Hmm, good idea.

335
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,140
I can't believe it.

336
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:49,577
We checked every stand in town, and
not one of them has that new Atori car.

337
00:17:49,660 --> 00:17:52,237
No wonder it's such a
prized bird around here.

338
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:54,040
Wait, prized? That's it?

339
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:57,270
Yogi!

340
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:01,097
That's what the old man meant! Say what?

341
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:02,540
Come here, look.

342
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:04,760
It's an announcement of a contest.

343
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:06,560
Fame, glory,

344
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:11,217
and the prized Niwatori card await the
heroic warrior who can beat our champion.

345
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:15,580
Signed, the Grand Battle Chief and
Combat Outfitter of Shadow Coliseum.

346
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:18,930
Yes.

347
00:18:19,013 --> 00:18:19,860
Let's sign up.

348
00:18:20,060 --> 00:18:21,942
I always wanted to be a warrior.

349
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:27,040
One of you as a Coliseum warrior?

350
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:28,377
I don't know.

351
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:32,020
This city takes its gladiator
matches quite seriously.

352
00:18:32,420 --> 00:18:35,185
What if it's a shot at
the champion you desire?

353
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:36,190
One moment.

354
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:43,080
Far be it from me to standing your way.

355
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:46,220
Here, your battle mask and combat cape.

356
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:50,080
Wow, is all this stuff really necessary?

357
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:54,917
Yes, if you're going to lose all your life
points, you may as well look like a hero.

358
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,300
All of my life points?

359
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:58,127
Give that stuff to me, Hugh.

360
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:00,253
What do you mean, Joey?

361
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:03,497
I'm not letting you risk all
your life points for this, pal.

362
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:04,997
I'll fight there, champion.

363
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:08,557
But Joey, you already have less
life points than both Mokuba and me.

364
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:09,470
Yeah.

365
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:13,377
Well, looks like I'm just gonna
have to be extra careful then, huh?

366
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:17,660
But so will the champ once he
sees the skills that I have. Okay.

367
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:19,180
Hey, thanks, Joey.

368
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:21,540
Forget about it.

369
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:24,700
Being a hero is what I do best. Come on!

370
00:19:24,980 --> 00:19:27,997
Bring it on! Let's see it! Let's see it!

371
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:29,520
Ladies and gentlemen,

372
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:34,018
we have at last found the soul brave
enough to challenge our champion.

373
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:38,680
I present to you the purveyor of
boundings, the picture of pugnacity,

374
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,520
the pig that backs a punch.

375
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:45,460
Introducing the challenger
that I've got, Senor Barty.

376
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:48,960
More like Senor Dorky to me.

377
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:52,612
No joke, the champ will have
a field day with this oinker.

378
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,917
Better than being called a lap dog.

379
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,780
Come on, Joey!

380
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:58,060
You can do it!

381
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:04,620
Now, introducing our undefeated champ,
the monarch of mayhem, the queen of fiend,

382
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:06,220
Madame Butterfly!

383
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:09,230
Whoa!

384
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:10,820
The champion's a girl!

385
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:15,300
And from the looks of it,
she's ready to rumble!

386
00:20:15,820 --> 00:20:17,040
Roast that pig!
